// TEST: A Stored Section Over Generic Float32 Cells Is Refused With A Span (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3020 @ 11:36
// ERROR-CONTAINS: the map's cells are Float32, but its kernel returns a Float64 value
// ============================================================================
// R11: a section bound as a value is lifted over Float64 parameters, so the
// kernel returned a double into a Float32 map and g++ refused the narrowing
// (BL9002). Refused at the kernel's call instead. (functions/913 is the
// Float64 twin.)
// ============================================================================
function outer(b) = {
    let f = (+)
    method_for(b) <@> lambda(v) -> f(v, v) |> compute
}
let r = outer([1.5, 2.5])